---
description: Resolve GetIt/needle dependencies with explicit type arguments
globs: "**/di/**/*.dart"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Explicit `sl<T>()` types

Always pass an explicit type argument when resolving from the service locator (`sl` / GetIt via `needle`). Do not rely on Dart inference with bare `sl()`.

## Why

Inference works for constructor arguments but fails when you chain (e.g. `sl().isOnline`) or when the expected type is unclear. Explicit types keep DI readable and consistent.

## Do

```dart
() => FavouritesProvider(
  getFavourites: sl<GetFavouritesUseCase>(),
  toggleFavourite: sl<ToggleFavouriteUseCase>(),
)

isOnline: () => sl<ConnectivityChecker>().isOnline,
```

## Do not

```dart
() => FavouritesProvider(getFavourites: sl(), toggleFavourite: sl())
```

## Scope

Apply anywhere you resolve dependencies — injectors under `di/`, test DI helpers (`test_di.dart`), and routers — not only files matching this rule’s globs.
